// v1 — changes need a pull request approved by a project manager.
//
// RoomService runs rooms and quizzes from start to finish: lobby, settings,
// timers, collecting and grading answers, disconnects and votes.
// Rooms live in memory (behind a RoomRepository interface), so a restart of
// this service ends the rooms in progress.
//
// Callers: Gateway, for every player action.
// Calls out to: QuizService (GenerateQuiz),
//               ScoringService (StartQuiz, RecordRound, FinalizeQuiz),
//               MatchDataService (GetSyncStatus, to know who is ready).
//
// Rules every RPC follows:
//   - The user_id comes from the Gateway (from the checked Auth0 token),
//     never from the browser's message body.
//   - NOT_FOUND if the room doesn't exist.
//   - PERMISSION_DENIED if the user isn't in the room, or isn't the host
//     for host-only actions.
//
// Room limits: 2–8 players.
// Settings: 5–20 questions (default 10), 10–45 seconds each (default 20).

// Code generated by protoc-gen-go. DO NOT EDIT.
// versions:
// 	protoc-gen-go v1.36.12
// 	protoc        (unknown)
